{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>And Moses said.</b> He already said to them [i.e., this is a continuation of a prior command], like <b>and YHWH Elohim formed</b> (Genesis 2:7), and many are like this." "<b>And the word מלאו.</b> Its grammar is strange, for sometimes it is a transitive verb and sometimes intransitive, and the binyan is kal." "<b>And the sense of \"for each man upon his son.\"</b> Even if the one who worshipped is his son or his brother, they are to kill him, and the reward is that He will bestow blessing upon you — and this is <b>at that time YHWH set apart the tribe of Levi</b> (Deuteronomy 10:8). And the reason is that HaShem told him this reason at Mount Sinai; therefore it says <b>these are the generations of Aaron and Moses on the day YHWH spoke with Moses at Mount Sinai</b> (Numbers 3:1). And behold, when the Tabernacle was made, Aaron and his sons were set apart to serve HaShem, and likewise the Levites. Then was the dispute of Korah, for he was a firstborn, since HaShem took the Levites in place of the firstborn, that they should be consecrated — because they offered the burnt offerings and the shelamim, they slaughtered upon the altar that was made before the calf."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:39:57.340763476Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}